1.What is the difference between HTML and HTML5?

HTML5 is the latest version of HTML and provides:

Semantic tags
Multimedia support
Local storage
Better APIs


2.What are semantic tags?

Semantic tags describe the meaning of content clearly.
<header>
<footer>
<article>
<section>
<nav>


3.Difference between div and span

| div              | span                          |
| ---------------- | ----------------------------- |
| Block element    | Inline element                |
| Takes full width | Takes only content width      |
| Used for layout  | Used for small inline styling |



4.Difference between id and class?

| id            | class         |
| ------------- | ------------- |
| Unique        | Reusable      |
| Access with # | Access with . |


5.Web accessibility

Web accessibility means making applications usable for everyone, including people with disabilities. In React, I follow semantic HTML,
provide alt text for images, ensure keyboard navigation, use proper labels for form fields, and add ARIA attributes wherever necessary.



