1. Difference between Flexbox and Grid?

| Flexbox              | Grid               |
| -------------------- | ------------------ |
| One-dimensional      | Two-dimensional    |
| Row OR column        | Row AND column     |
| Better for alignment | Better for layouts |

Flexbox → Navbar/cards
Grid → Full page layouts/dashboard



2. What is CSS Box Model

Box model contains:

Content
Padding
Border
Margin

Total Width=Content+Padding+Border+Margin


3.Difference between relative, absolute, fixed, sticky?

| Position | Behavior                              |
| -------- | ------------------------------------- |
| relative | Relative to itself                    |
| absolute | Relative to nearest positioned parent |
| fixed    | Fixed to viewport                     |
| sticky   | Sticky during scroll                  |


4.What is z-index?

z-index controls stacking order of positioned elements.

Higher z-index appears on top.

5.CSS specificity

CSS specificity determines which CSS rule gets applied when multiple selectors target the same element. 
The priority is generally inline styles, IDs, classes, and then element selectors. For example, if an element has both a class and an ID selector,
the ID selector wins because it has higher specificity. If specificity is equal, the rule declared later usually takes precedence.

Inline → ID → Class → Element


